<meta type=article title="Minipage: a sealed frameable (#115)">
</meta>

<section | Private numbering and inbound references>

A document figure outside any box, on the document figure counter:

<fig #fig:doc src=doc.png | A document figure.>

A sealed minipage holding its own private figure. The figure inside counts
in the box's PRIVATE figure registry, so it is "Figure 1" even though a
document figure already exists — the document counter is untouched:

<minipage #mp:numbering +numbered caption="A sealed box with a private figure" |
The inner figure resolves within the box: <ref @fig:inner>.

<fig #fig:inner src=inner.png | An inner figure, numbered privately.>
>

The document figure is <ref @fig:doc>. An inbound reference to the box's
inner figure does not resolve — the body's labels never entered the
document registry, so it is a normal not-found ref-error: <ref @fig:inner>.

<section | Cross-referencing minipages>

A minipage gets its own outward label in the "Minipage N" series, so it is
itself cross-referenceable and one minipage's label can be referenced
alongside another's:

<minipage #mp:a +numbered caption="The first box" | First sealed box.>

<minipage #mp:b +numbered caption="The second box" | Second sealed box.>

The boxes are <ref @mp:a> and <ref @mp:b>.

<section | Box-local footnotes>

A footnote authored inside a minipage is collected at the box's own bottom
boundary (the LaTeX bottom-of-minipage behavior), not hoisted to the
document's notes:

<minipage #mp:notes +numbered caption="A box with a footnote" |
This box has a footnote.<note | The footnote is collected at the box bottom.>
>

<section | Nested minipages>

A minipage inside a minipage recurses within the deferred phase; each level
numbers in its own private registry:

<minipage #mp:outer +numbered caption="Outer box" |
Outer content.

<minipage #mp:inner +numbered caption="Inner box" |
Inner content with its own private figure: <fig #fig:nested src=nested.png | Nested figure.>
>
>

<section | External pulls are forbidden>

A minipage is self-contained: an `@src`/`<data>` external asset pull inside
the body is rejected with a visible error, never resolved:

<minipage #mp:guard | This box tries to pull an external asset: <fig src="@logo" | A logo.>>
